  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Low risk of a few severe storms today, mainly in SC.\n\nA stalled frontal boundary over/near the area will combine with \nmoderate instability and mid-level dry air to yield a low risk for a \nfew severe storms this aftn/eve, mainly in SC. Damaging wind gusts \nwill be the main severe wx hazard, although large hail and \neven excessive rainfall will also be possible.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Cooler and drier conditions to start the work week \nwill be followed by warmer and eventually wetter conditions late \nweek.\n\nHigh pressure building in from the north Mon will bring cooler and \ndrier air into the area to start the work week, especially inland. \nThe onshore winds and higher moisture near the coast should keep \nsome showers around, mainly near the SC coast. Humidity will then \nincrease again late week as high pressure moves offshore allowing \nsoutherly winds to return ahead of another cold front.",
